# Flutter Project Structure

Follow these guidelines for organizing Flutter projects:

## Project Organization
- Use web-assembly first
- Use a clean, modular architecture (MVVM, Clean Architecture, BLoC pattern, etc.)
- Organize code by feature rather than by type
- Keep UI separate from business logic
- Use proper dependency injection
- Follow the appropriate directory structure

## Package Organization
- Keep a clean dependency graph
- Use packages for reusable components
- Follow semantic versioning for packages
- Group related functionality in the same package
- Use package visibility modifiers appropriately

## Module Organization
- Split large modules into submodules
- Use barrel files (index.dart) for cleaner imports
- Keep modules focused on specific functionality
- Use interfaces to define module boundaries
- Document module responsibilities

## Naming Conventions
- Use lowercase_with_underscores for file names
- Use camelCase for variable and method names
- Use PascalCase for class names
- Use lowercase_with_underscores for package names
- Keep names descriptive and concise

## Asset Organization
- Organize assets by type and purpose
- Use proper naming for asset files
- Add appropriate resolution variants for images
- Document asset usage
- Optimize assets for production 